# TEMPLATE — copy to `client-patterns.local` and fill in.
#
#   cp .githooks/client-patterns.local.example .githooks/client-patterns.local
#
# `client-patterns.local` is GITIGNORED and must stay that way. This repo is
# PUBLIC, so committing the real list would publish exactly the names the hook
# exists to keep out — the guard would become the leak.
#
# One case-insensitive extended-regex per line. `\b` gives word boundaries so a
# short name does not match inside unrelated words. Blank lines and #-comments
# are ignored.
#
# Cover, for each engagement: company name, common abbreviations and former
# names, site/campus names, and any internal system name that is not a public
# product.

\bExampleCorp\b
\bExmplCo\b
\bNorthCampus\b
